{"schema_version":1,"observation_id":"events-0e83444efd1940a497edd73175fb6231","run_id":"t1-t7-gpt-5-nano-high-t4-swipe-to-seek-linux-run-047e07a9e893","after":3811,"next_sequence":3850,"events":[{"sequence":3812,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T18:09:53.472958Z","elapsed_seconds":216.909,"source":"pi","event":{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering feedback display changes**\n\nI want to enhance the PlaybackController with a \"seekFeedback\" property to show a text overlay, which isn't currently available. Instead of using the center HUD, I\u2019m thinking of implementing a \"bottom overlay\" with the \"HeroFeedbackSurface\" during seeking. To do this, I'll add a \"SeekOverlay\" debug status in \"VoidScreen\" using a \"ValueNotifier\" for tracking seeking. I'll also update \"HeroFeedbackSurface\" to provide live feedback while dragging through the overlay.\n\n**Implementing seeking feedback**\n\nI'm planning to add a `seekFeedbackNotifier` in `playback_controller.dart` as a `ValueNotifier<SeekFeedback?>`. This will track seeking details through the `SeekFeedback` class, which includes position, duration, and target. I\u2019ll also define a state class for managing seeking status.\n\nTo simplify things even further, I\u2019ll introduce `SeekOverlayInfo`, which stores position and duration in milliseconds. Additionally, I want to modify `HeroFeedbackSurface` to accept the `PlaybackController` so it can adjust based on user interactions during seeking.\n\n**Accessing PlaybackController**\n\nI realize I can access `PlaybackController` directly from `HeroFeedbackSurface`, thanks to the `onSeek` callback and functions like `positionMs` and `durationMs`. To keep everything organized, I\u2019ll modify `onSeekStart`, `onSeekUpdate`, and `onSeekEnd` to update `seekFeedbackNotifier`. \n\nSince we can't reach `PlaybackController` globally, I\u2019ll add a `SeekFeedbackUpdater` parameter to `HeroFeedbackSurface`. Meanwhile, I also plan to introduce a callback for `onSeekProgress` to track the current target during gestures. I\u2019ll need to check where `HeroFeedbackSurface` is utilized next.\n\n**Modifying HeroFeedbackSurface use**\n\nIn `VoidScreen`, `HeroFeedbackSurface` wraps the hero area, and I see how it\u2019s structured in the `buildHeroGestureSurface` code. I\u2019ll enhance this by adding an `onSeekPreview` parameter to update the bottom bar with `SeekOverlayInfo`. \n\nWhen modifying `HeroFeedbackSurface`, I'll make sure to call `onSeekPreview` within `onSeekStart` for the seeking info. The target will be calculated in `onSeekUpdate`, and I\u2019ll also ensure the overlay clears after the gesture ends to maintain a smooth user experience.\n\n**Designing the seek overlay**\n\nI\u2019m planning to set `onSeekEnd` to either clear the seek preview or invoke it with a null value to signal that seeking has stopped. The UI will read the \"seek preview\" in `VoidScreen`, and I'll create a small row overlay that sits just above the progress hairline. \n\nA new `ValueNotifier<SeekOverlayInfo?>` will be added to `PlaybackController` to handle updates during seeking. In `VoidScreen`, I\u2019ll use a `Selector` or `ValueListenableBuilder` to display the target, duration, and progress in a consistent format above the hairline, ensuring everything flows smoothly.\n\n**Finalizing overlay positioning**\n\nTo ensure the overlay appears correctly above the hairline, I'll set its position using `m.reservedBottom + overlayHeight` so it\u2019s visible. The hairline height is only 1 dp, so using `bottom: m.reservedBottom + 2` creates the necessary space. Instead of modifying the existing structure, I\u2019m thinking about wrapping the hairline within a stack. \n\nI\u2019ll define a function for the bottom overlay HUD that reads from a `ValueNotifier<SeekOverlayInfo?>`, extending `PlaybackController` to manage seek events effectively. I\u2019ll also adjust the callback in `HeroFeedbackSurface` to incorporate these updates seamlessly.\n\n**Implementing Seek Overlay**\n\nI need to pass the `PlaybackController` from `MediaControllerPage` down to `VoidScreen` using `ChangeNotifierProvider`. In `VoidScreen`, I'll access it via `context.read<PlaybackController>()` to handle the `seekOverlayNotifier`. \n\nWe\u2019ll define the `SeekOverlayInfo` class and set up a `ValueNotifier` in `PlaybackController` to track seek updates. Then, I'll update `HeroFeedbackSurface` to use an optional parameter for `onSeekPreview`, which will allow it to update the overlay when seeking. I'll ensure that we can handle null values appropriately to clear the overlay when seeking ends.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_09626669b9b7f964016a8dda428ccc8197a31c737109d4aefd\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqjdprDujvEtB243yIixrNuRQ5mMpMF2M2bS76vrg_UHm9XC_8k634mGE2aG58RCSRaI1-S6nhU4PZkGZGaFMOJWbz-t5r_0GKLkfbj383wrpMLm6W-_-Hxp8XW6G4GqVhk3p4jFw0tEoX2GfYbCvsBWvB9DDAKXUVIHXKnFHVTBgsD5qkgm9UmwgckXh0nX1ZQoImvRV0ZmJNEzt_EFlBZFNuLsRH5eDvGQ4ONQzAEViF7DGvGmc2M1RWOkvRxlvApNFkEGJU_iRpnvV4H5jsMdx3YJw8SYMzIAFyRE64ocWEdnfqig0ZjzxQ75QFu10BexT-_Qgwk8tAsKyRa0qqlPIpDg_ue8UNDkCt8p9OL1ltFVx5hcLZa8qc-T78uVxyGuxnPHCGVGTq6QInXfdxwt8qgCglq34sYRhDhBl09t2W-azCvDAuIZ_JySUNlRwNLEW24vAY4Rpv24cNYgWCJmKlOE3w0xpteFIFuXGSN1mYRj_vXATInKnQQ6CqzLoQRC6X7q4gva7_cUZExEXQsfVmWojUZeyn9qvkIbLJmtuTzULhc2U5s7Ds9ecwNH_oZ6CKzJJkhMcjH_GbOYBknNoaR6AM-2-U7hyd8iaWyLuvix7KYnwDl_hEjflep0hRd56enlDpW0SliHvlRYGYEd8CM7i-OUv9Zl5mMOQvaAznH14OLqLycorLcZsZES14C9YvoOoA1Xrg6ek0BRR57KnDiSELermZzn7fZgqW6P3whXEOejlgNcCKdpTgckSTflVEjToUCZ3yQUxanZOaekTf-aWl7jhJPSWym7sI1uRNYcauieZXlBFEiMgWQXj6CTCTpIKnwZ_zSQZx6x9JKvkUfiRtKAUG4NMfSuT-JygLHB_wsnXDlnyqiJno1qlX2jaPQ1Y5YPfpJmIL1VV0Gtkb2Ni2_zij9InnwA2TiNR1uCss_XDhI_BkU2tS0X0x7rrcsbkhPFwMzh1jyD2dCzi-cxjRb-Iog2uCMFxfqr--yf6DUlBlMp3zNPBw6Y5jJkrePxqZ2ClHEHYk2DoJsamvmCXBgTcpz2EX1eXwujlGURAKE5uYmdrCqbLg7YVFO0i6zQjZBmi2hxKceuNeXjCUXDWMWKugjQK-uWqDg7lYa8CIivH8-HbTSX7ozpE-jQsFx-jOwLFteCBb